💭 An object that is handed to a call wrapped in 🔺, which keeps it.
💭
💭 Expected: the program prints "kept: balloon".
💭 What happens: see README.md. The compiler does not look at the arguments of a call
💭 that is wrapped in 🔺 (ASTReraise::analyseMemoryFlow), so it never learns that the
💭 object leaves through it, and places the object in the caller's frame.
💭
💭 Handling the error where the call is made is fine: 🆗 kept 🐻 basket fresh❗️ 🍇 … 🍉 🙅‍♀️ error 🍇 … 🍉.
